    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Symptomatic neonates:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " PGE1 infusion (starting 0.05–0.1 mcg/kg/min) reopens the constricted ductus to stabilize them before early surgery."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "After a response, reduce to the lowest rate that holds it (0.1 → 0.05 → 0.025 → 0.01 mcg/kg/min); if 0.05 isn't enough, up to 0.4 mcg/kg/min (higher rates usually add nothing)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " apnea in about 10–12% of neonates (most often < 2 kg, usually in the first hour); monitor breathing and have ventilatory support at hand. > 120 h of therapy: watch for gastric outlet obstruction (antral hyperplasia). Long infusions: cortical proliferation of long bones (regresses after stopping)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Overdose signs:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " apnea, bradycardia, pyrexia, hypotension, flushing. Apnea or bradycardia: stop the infusion; fever or hypotension: slow it."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
